    "reasoning_content": "Let me now analyze all the upcoming events/tasks with dates between now and end of 2026. Let me list them chronologically:\n\n**July 2026:**\n- Sat Jul 18: \"go feebee church\" at 16:00 (4pm)\n- Sat Jul 18: \"pick up feebeee\" at 15:45 (3:45pm)\n- Sat Jul 18: \"dinner with feebee church friends\" at 19:00 (7pm)\n- Sun Jul 19: \"Jarod's confirmation ceremony\" at 11:30am (UTC 03:30)\n- Sun Jul 19: \"study with feebee\" at 14:00 (2pm)\n- Sun Jul 19: \"Stay over Zacs house\" at 20:00 (8pm)\n- Mon Jul 20: \"Watch WC finals with AC\" at 03:00 (3am)\n- Mon Jul 20: \"round 1 coursereg\" (all day)\n- Wed Jul 22: \"Run and dinner with Ethan\" at 19:00 (7pm)\n- Thu Jul 23: \"Huixin farewell dinner\" at 19:00 (7pm)\n- Sat Jul 25: \"car picnic with feebee\" at 19:00 (7pm)\n- Sat Jul 25: \"AG\" at 16:00 (4pm) - recurring every Saturday\n- Mon Jul 27: \"Deadline to redeem Starbucks stars\" (all day)\n- Tue Jul 28: \"round 2 coursereg\" (all day)\n- Thu Jul 30: \"Let prof know about IT1244 TA\" (all day)\n\n**August 2026:**\n- Sat Aug 1: \"talk with feebee\" at 19:00 (7pm)\n- Sat Aug 1: \"AG\" (recurring every Saturday at 4pm)\n- Mon Aug 3: \"round 3 coursereg\" (all day)\n- Wed Aug 5: \"Spiderman brand new day with feebee\" at 18:00 (6pm)\n- Tue Aug 11: \"round 1 tutorial reg\" (all day)\n- Every Saturday: \"AG\" at 4pm\n\n**September 2026:**\n- Fri Sep 4: \"AG Retreat (Day 1)\" (all day)\n- Sat Sep 5: \"AG Retreat (Day 2)\" (all day)\n- Sun Sep 6: \"AG Retreat (Day 3)\" (all day)\n- Every Saturday: \"AG\" at 4pm\n\n**October 2026:**\n- Sat Oct 3: \"undo apple tv subscription\" (all day)\n- Every Saturday: \"AG\" at 4pm\n\n**November 2026:**\n- Sun Nov 1: \"nic yap bday\" (all day, recurring)\n- Every Saturday: \"AG\" at 4pm\n\n**December 2026:**\n- Sun Dec 20: \"feebee birthday\" (all day, recurring)\n- Every Saturday: \"AG\" at 4pm\n\nNow let me think about maximizing overseas time with 10 leave days. I need to find the longest contiguous period. The strategy is:\n- Use 10 working days of leave\n- Leverage weekends (Sat/Sun) which don't count as leave\n- Find the best window with minimal conflicts\n\nThe key constraint periods based on events:\n- Late July has lots of events\n- Aug 4-5 has events\n- Aug 11 has round 1 tutorial reg\n- Sep 4-6: AG Retreat (3 days)\n- Every Saturday has \"AG\" at 4pm (recurring)\n\nNow, let me think about the best window. Let me look at windows between events:\n\nLet me think about this from the perspective of finding the longest possible contiguous block.\n\nThe \"AG\" recurring every Saturday is a problem - it happens every single Saturday at 4pm. And \"AG Retreat\" is Sep 4-6 (Fri-Sun).\n\nBut the user asked me to maximize overseas time. These are existing commitments. Let me find the best window.\n\nLet me think about what constitutes a \"blocked\" day. A single 2-hour event doesn't necessarily block the whole day for overseas travel, but the user is asking about going overseas - they can't be in Singapore for these events if they're overseas.\n\nLet me think about the windows:\n\n**Window 1: Starting after the busy late-July / early-August period**\n\nAfter Aug 5 (\"Spiderman brand new day with feebee\"), the next hard commitment is:\n- Aug 11: \"round 1 tutorial reg\" \n- Then every Saturday: \"AG\" at 4pm\n- Sep 4-6: \"AG Retreat\"\n\nSo the gap from Aug 6 to Sep 3:\n- Aug 6 (Thu) to Sep 3 (Thu) = 29 days\n\nLet me count working days: Aug 6 is Thursday.\n\nWeek 1: Aug 6 (Thu), Aug 7 (Fri) - 2 days, weekend Aug 8-9\nWeek 2: Aug 10-14 - 5 days, weekend Aug 15-16\nWeek 3: Aug 17-21 - 5 days, weekend Aug 22-23\nWeek 4: Aug 24-28 - 5 days, weekend Aug 29-30\nWeek 5: Aug 31 - Sep 3 (Mon-Thu) - 4 days\n\nThat's 2+5+5+5+4 = 21 working days. But we only have 10 leave days.\n\nWith 10 leave days, the maximum overseas time would be: take 10 consecutive working days that span across weekends.\n\nThe optimal pattern with 10 leave days:\n- Start on a Friday evening or Saturday\n- Take leave Mon-Fri (Week 1): 5 days, covered by weekend before and after → 9 calendar days\n- Take leave Mon-Fri (Week 2): 5 days, covered by weekend → another 7 calendar days\n- Total: 16 calendar days (Sat to Sun across two full weeks)\n\nOr even: \n- Start Fri: Take Fri (1), then Mon-Fri (5), Mon-Wed (3), Thu (1) = 10 days\n- This spans: Fri to the following Thu = about 14 days + weekends\n\nWait, let me think more carefully. The optimal is:\n\n10 consecutive working days (Mon-Fri, Mon-Fri) spanning 3 weekends:\n- Sat-Sun (weekend before) + Mon-Fri (5 leave days) + Sat-Sun (weekend) + Mon-Fri (5 leave days) + Sat-Sun (weekend after)\n= 2 + 5 + 2 + 5 + 2 = 16 calendar days\n\nSo the maximum is 16 calendar days with exactly 10 leave days.\n\nNow, is there a 16-day window with no conflicts?\n\nLet me check the best windows:\n\n**Window A: Aug 6 (Thu) to Aug 21 (Fri)** - 16 days\nBut wait, Aug 6 is Thursday - not ideal for the weekend-start pattern.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The leave days don't have to be perfectly Mon-Fri x 2. The optimal is to use 10 leave days on working days, maximizing the span between weekends.\n\nThe absolute maximum span:\n- Start on a Saturday (before the first leave day) \n- Use leave on 10 working days\n- End on a Sunday (after the last leave day)\n\nThe best case: 10 working days across 2 weeks + 3 weekends. That's 16 days.\n\nNow, what about starting mid-week and using some leave days differently?\n\nLet me look at the actual calendar:\n\nLet me consider the window **after Aug 5**:\n\nAug 6 (Thu) - leave 1\nAug 7 (Fri) - leave 2\nAug 8-9 (Sat-Sun) - weekend\nAug 10 (Mon) - leave 3\nAug 11 (Tue) - \"round 1 tutorial reg\" - CONFLICT\n...\n\nSo Aug 11 is a conflict. Let me see if this can be worked around.\n\nWindow **after Aug 11**:\nAug 12 (Wed) - leave 1\nAug 13 (Thu) - leave 2\nAug 14 (Fri) - leave 3\nAug 15-16 (Sat-Sun) - weekend\nAug 17 (Mon) - leave 4\nAug 18 (Tue) - leave 5\nAug 19 (Wed) - leave 6\nAug 20 (Thu) - leave 7\nAug 21 (Fri